  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kenya IDF Strengthening the Use of Country Safeguards Systems</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this IDF grant is to strengthen country system capacity in the areas of environmental and social safeguards in Kenya.  The grant will finance a two year program designed to build capacity to assess, manage and monitor the environmental and social safeguards risks in development projects to reduce the negative externalities of large-scale infrastructure investments and other targeted interventions across core growth sectors. The grant will permit the GoK to determine where current safeguards capacities lie as well as identify key gaps in government capabilities regarding safeguards assessment, planning, monitoring and management within and across ministries. Grant funds will be earmarked for baseline diagnostic work as well as activities to strengthen incentives for adopting best practice with respect to safeguards processes and tools as well as provide support for skills enhancement and training among government technical staff tasked with application and oversight of investment project safeguards.</narrative>
  </description>
